Aerie-Purpose: Lock Helium's layout to the sidebar and Zen mode off in the pref service itself, so the user, Settings, sync, an extension or an old profile cannot change them.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/prefs (chrome_command_line_pref_store.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #215, item 6 (ADR 0008). One call in the constructor of ChromeCommandLinePrefStore, the command-line layer of
every PrefService Chrome builds. aerie_sidebar::LockHeliumLayout (overlay, components/aerie_sidebar) puts
helium.browser.layout = vertical and helium.browser.zen_mode = false into it. A value in that layer wins over the
user's own file, so Helium's code, which reads the effective pref, sees the sidebar layout whatever was written
before, and PrefService::Preference::IsUserModifiable() is false for both prefs. A write changes only the user store
and no observer runs, so nothing is written back. This replaces the write-back hold that sidebar/0021 used to carry in
HeliumLayoutStateController.

The Local State service builds the same store and gets the two values too; neither pref is registered there, and the
service only reads registered prefs.

--- a/chrome/browser/prefs/chrome_command_line_pref_store.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/prefs/chrome_command_line_pref_store.cc
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 #include "chrome/common/chrome_switches.h"
 #include "chrome/common/pref_names.h"
+#include "components/aerie_sidebar/aerie_sidebar_layout_lock.h"
 #include "components/browser_sync/browser_sync_switches.h"
 #include "components/language/core/browser/pref_names.h"
 #include "components/proxy_config/proxy_config_dictionary.h"
@@ -111,6 +112,8 @@
   ApplySSLSwitches();
   ApplyBackgroundModeSwitches();
   ApplyExplicitlyAllowedPortSwitch();
+  // Aerie: the layout is the sidebar and Zen mode is off, for good (ADR 0008).
+  aerie_sidebar::LockHeliumLayout(this);
 }
 
 ChromeCommandLinePrefStore::~ChromeCommandLinePrefStore() = default;
